{
  "Name": "Okta - Authentication & Sessions - Attempted Bypass of Okta MFA",
  "Description": "Alert: Alert - Okta - Authentication & Sessions\nMITRE ATT&CK: Credential Access / T1111\nSchedule: every 15 minutes over the previous 15 minutes (edit the scheduled search to change it)\nTuning: okta_user_allowlist / okta_ip_allowlist keys \"<login without domain>|Attempted Bypass of Okta MFA\" or \"<ip>|Attempted Bypass of Okta MFA\"\n\nDetects attempts to bypass Okta multi-factor authentication (MFA). An adversary may attempt to bypass the Okta MFA policies configured for an organization in order to obtain unauthorized access to an application.\n\nReference(s):\n- https://detection.fyi/elastic/detection-rules/integrations/okta/credential_access_attempted_bypass_of_okta_mfa/\n- https://github.com/elastic/detection-rules/tree/main/rules/integrations/okta/credential_access_attempted_bypass_of_okta_mfa.toml",
  "Labels": [
    "okta",
    "detection",
    "authentication-sessions",
    "credential-access",
    "T1111"
  ],
  "Schedule": "13,28,43,58 * * * *",
  "Duration": -900,
  "DefaultDeploymentRules": {
    "Disabled": false,
    "RunImmediately": false
  },
